@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mw-s1-definitions`

-- PUBLISHED FIGURES, NOT LAW. The Minimum Wage Law states the rule that produces the minimum wage
-- (47.5 percent of the average wage, increased under s 4) but, apart from the 1987 amounts of s 21,
-- not the shekel figure. The figure in force is published by the Minister under s 6 and by the National
-- Insurance Institute. The two amounts below are the ones row IL-05 took from the Institute's minimum
-- wage page and recorded with their provenance (IL-05 nii-il05-published-figures.l4, lines 68-83, and its
-- NOTES.md section 7); they are reused here and not re-fetched. Nothing here was fetched by this row.
--
--   page: https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a8%20%d7%9e%d7%99%d7%a0%d7%99%d7%9e%d7%95%d7%9d.aspx
--   fetched by IL-05 on 2026-10-06 at 14:52:49Z, sha256 0c7ff9205881f9b13396791c2b058bb511b1ec2e51bd6a9cb9ae20effa5ac743
--   what it prints (IL-05 transcription): "minimum wage from age 18 and over", monthly 6,443.85 NIS
--   (from 01.04.2026); in its table, 6,247.67 (from 01.04.2025).
--
-- The Institute describes its content as general information and not the binding text of the Law; each
-- figure here is an official publication of a computed amount, not law.
--
-- The average wage is published too (IL-05 nii-il05-published-figures.l4, "The average wage from 1 January
-- 2026"): 13,566 NIS under s 1 of the National Insurance Law, from 01.01.2026 (page
-- https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a8%20%d7%9e%d7%9e%d7%95%d7%a6%d7%a2.aspx,
-- fetched 2026-10-06 14:49:57Z, sha256 0afd95b65113a99dfc9bb9cd277090a927d26fa0c39b49a75be4ec1931829532).
-- It is used here only to cross-check the Law's 47.5 percent against the published 6,443.85 (the tests).
--
-- The Law's own editorial note after the definition prints "from April 2023, 5,571.75 NIS per month"
-- (src:23, an aid, not authority). It names no end date, and the period between it and 1 April 2025
-- saw further updates (s 4, s 6) that no source held by this row prints, so no answer is given for a
-- day between 1 April 1988 and 31 March 2025 (the refusal below). Before that, the Law's own s 21 prints 525 and 551.

§ `Minimum wage figures published by the Minister and the National Insurance Institute — not encoded law`

@ref National Insurance Institute, "minimum wage", fetched 2026-10-06 by row IL-05 (sha256 above); s 1 "שכר מינימום" (source line 23)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2025, as published` MEANS 6_247.67

@ref National Insurance Institute, "minimum wage", fetched 2026-10-06 by row IL-05 (sha256 above); s 1 "שכר מינימום" (source line 23)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published` MEANS 6_443.85

@ref National Insurance Institute, "average wage under section 1", fetched 2026-10-06 by row IL-05 (sha256 above); s 1 "שכר מינימום" (source line 23)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage from 1 January 2026, as published` MEANS 13_566

@ref s 1 "שכר מינימום" (source line 23): the update is made on 1 April each year, and the next one had not been published when IL-05 fetched its pages on 2026-10-06
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the full monthly minimum wage from 1 April 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched` MEANS
    REFUSE "the full monthly minimum wage from 1 April 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched"

@ref the sources held by this row print no figure for a day before 1 April 2025 (see the header)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025` MEANS
    REFUSE "no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025"

-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED (NOTES.md F6): a figure published for 1 April holds until the next 1 April,
-- the day s 1 updates it; a rise under s 4 within the year would appear in the Institute's table,
-- and IL-05 recorded none between 1 April 2025 and 1 April 2026.
-- The same assumption carries s 21(a)(2)'s 551 from 1 October 1987 to 31 March 1988 (s 21(a)(2)
-- says it does not detract from s 4, so an increase under s 4 may have intervened: not held).
-- From 1 April 1988 to 31 March 2025 the text prints no figure and no publication is held: declined.
-- Where two adjacent figures are held, s 5 applies: the later never falls below the earlier.
@ref s 1 "שכר מינימום" (source line 23), s 6(1) (source line 54), s 21(a) (source lines 175-176), s 5 (source line 50)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE  @desc the day asked about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over on` `the day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2027 4 1) THEN `the full monthly minimum wage from 1 April 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2026 4 1) THEN `the monthly minimum wage after an update, given` `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2025, as published` `and` `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2025 4 1) THEN `the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2025, as published`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 1988 4 1) THEN `no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 1987 10 1) THEN `the monthly minimum wage after an update, given` `the monthly minimum wage that section 21(a)(1) fixes for 1 April 1987` `and` `the monthly minimum wage that section 21(a)(2) fixes for 1 October 1987`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 1987 4 1) THEN `the monthly minimum wage that section 21(a)(1) fixes for 1 April 1987`
           -- before 1 April 1987 (s 20, line 170) the Law had not commenced; the same refusal serves, as no source prints a figure
           OTHERWISE `no source held by this model prints the full monthly minimum wage before 1 April 2025`
